("Hall of Fame" by The Script)

00:13:15.489 --> 00:13:16.933
- So thank you guys, again, for watching.

00:13:16.933 --> 00:13:18.040
I believe in you.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:19.892
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:13:19.892 --> 00:13:23.102
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:13:23.102 --> 00:13:24.602
I'll see you soon.

00:13:30.483 --> 00:13:33.641
- Personal training is a
very, very rewarding job,

00:13:33.641 --> 00:13:34.782
in more ways than one.

00:13:34.782 --> 00:13:36.953
You can make decent money
as a personal trainer,

00:13:36.953 --> 00:13:38.743
but it's not about the money.

00:13:38.743 --> 00:13:40.534
It's about, really, changing these lives,

00:13:40.534 --> 00:13:41.663
like, touching lives.

00:13:41.663 --> 00:13:44.913
I've had people, I had
a woman who I helped,

00:13:44.913 --> 00:13:47.555
I helped her lose a hundred pounds.

00:13:47.555 --> 00:13:51.047
She was like this, she was
an obese, morbidly obese.

00:13:51.047 --> 00:13:54.501
And when I was done with her,
she was a hot, fit chick.

00:13:54.501 --> 00:13:55.543
There was a old guy.

00:13:55.543 --> 00:13:56.376
I loved this guy.

00:13:56.376 --> 00:13:57.464
He was in his 70's.

00:13:57.464 --> 00:14:00.622
Very, very sedentary lifestyle.

00:14:00.622 --> 00:14:02.303
With him, it wasn't about
the lifting weights.

00:14:02.303 --> 00:14:04.935
We did a few things for
resistance training,

00:14:04.935 --> 00:14:07.516
but, you know, I threw
some boxing gloves on 'em,

00:14:07.516 --> 00:14:09.315
and held mitts, and it gave him life.

00:14:09.315 --> 00:14:10.256
He loved it.

00:14:10.256 --> 00:14:13.013
So, you find what these people want to do.

00:14:13.013 --> 00:14:15.132
You find somethin' that works for them,

00:14:15.132 --> 00:14:16.336
somethin' that's going
to keep them healthy,

00:14:16.336 --> 00:14:19.204
alive, and vibrant, and then
you run with that, you know?

00:14:19.204 --> 00:14:21.503
So, it was very rewarding in that sense.

00:14:21.503 --> 00:14:23.421
Well, like I said, overproduce.

00:14:23.421 --> 00:14:26.243
Whatever your role is, do more.

00:14:26.243 --> 00:14:27.984
I don't care if you work at McDonald's.

00:14:27.984 --> 00:14:29.081
Do more.

00:14:29.081 --> 00:14:30.443
Because, what you're doing,

00:14:30.443 --> 00:14:33.153
is you're making yourself important.

00:14:33.153 --> 00:14:35.316
You're not going to be the
guy, when budgets need to be,

00:14:35.316 --> 00:14:37.287
when budget cuts are on a table,

00:14:37.287 --> 00:14:38.993
your name is not even going
to be in the conversation.

00:14:38.993 --> 00:14:40.535
Out, we need him.

00:14:40.535 --> 00:14:42.047
Everybody else, you know what I mean?

00:14:42.047 --> 00:14:46.467
And, you're developing an
impeccable work capacity,

00:14:46.467 --> 00:14:50.583
and ethic, which, if you
ever do become your own boss,

00:14:50.583 --> 00:14:52.095
or manager, or whatever,

00:14:52.095 --> 00:14:55.752
you already have that
achievement unlocked already.

00:14:55.752 --> 00:14:56.585
You know what I mean?

00:14:56.585 --> 00:14:58.486
So, that's somethin' that
you definitely want to do.

00:14:58.486 --> 00:14:59.819
So, overdevelop.

00:15:01.017 --> 00:15:02.929
And I tell people, it's
about bein' a winner.

00:15:02.929 --> 00:15:06.396
You know, my supplement
company's called I'm So Alpha.

00:15:06.396 --> 00:15:08.566
I didn't come up with that, you know?

00:15:08.566 --> 00:15:11.268
I will put stuff out, like
pictures and videos, and stuff,

00:15:11.268 --> 00:15:12.839
and like, people would just hashtag, like,

00:15:12.839 --> 00:15:14.069
"That's so alpha.

00:15:14.069 --> 00:15:15.509
"So f***** alpha.

00:15:15.509 --> 00:15:16.548
"We love that s***."

00:15:16.548 --> 00:15:18.066
It's just a mind state, right?

00:15:18.066 --> 00:15:19.311
So, and when I say that, like,

00:15:19.311 --> 00:15:21.930
people think, oh, that's
super arrogant and cocky.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.258
It's not.

00:15:23.258 --> 00:15:25.557
There's nothin' wrong with
bein' confident, for one,

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:28.779
because (clears throat)
when you are legitimate,

00:15:28.779 --> 00:15:31.060
when you really, like, qualify yourself,

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:33.382
in whatever field you're in, you know,

00:15:33.382 --> 00:15:36.322
and you handle business, you
got the work to show for it,

00:15:36.322 --> 00:15:38.229
why not be confident, you know?

00:15:38.229 --> 00:15:40.392
Some people mistake that
for arrogance, or cockiness.

00:15:40.392 --> 00:15:41.570
I'm not about that.

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:43.132
You know, I'm about
bein' confident, though.

00:15:43.132 --> 00:15:46.020
I can't help it, you know?

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.640
So, you conduct yourself in a certain way.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.942
So, it's a whole lifestyle that I push,

00:15:50.942 --> 00:15:52.818
with the type of training that I do.

00:15:52.818 --> 00:15:55.064
You know, it goes into my everyday life.

00:15:55.064 --> 00:15:56.001
I can't help it.

00:15:56.001 --> 00:15:58.642
You know, that's why the
company's I'm So Alpha.

00:15:58.642 --> 00:16:01.400
I hashtag, and I got shirts
that say, Alpha as ****.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.524
It's like, I'm really
going to ****** do this,

00:16:03.524 --> 00:16:04.357
you know what I mean?

00:16:04.357 --> 00:16:07.200
Whatever it is, anything,
like, any kind of challenge,

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.989
I'm like, I want to do it.

00:16:08.989 --> 00:16:09.822
I want to do it.

00:16:09.822 --> 00:16:10.655
Oh, that's hard?

00:16:10.655 --> 00:16:12.337
Yeah, I think, okay, let me do it.

00:16:12.337 --> 00:16:14.202
I'mma do it harder, and I'mma, you know?

00:16:14.202 --> 00:16:15.514
Add more weight, and I'mma do it,

00:16:15.514 --> 00:16:16.347
you know what I'm sayin'?

00:16:16.347 --> 00:16:18.590
So, you know, it just, mentally,

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:20.477
it sets you up for life, to be a winner,

00:16:20.477 --> 00:16:21.887
'cause I'm all about bein' a winner.

00:16:21.887 --> 00:16:23.748
And I'm not talkin' about on stage.

00:16:23.748 --> 00:16:25.434
That's not really winning, is it?

00:16:25.434 --> 00:16:26.935
You know, it's not a competition.

00:16:26.935 --> 00:16:29.744
You're just gettin' judged,
by people who don't lift,

00:16:29.744 --> 00:16:30.577
you know what I'm sayin'?

00:16:30.577 --> 00:16:32.534
(group laughing)

00:16:32.534 --> 00:16:36.504
Winning in life, winning
in life is like...

00:16:36.504 --> 00:16:39.581
Winning in life is like, you know,

00:16:39.581 --> 00:16:42.620
your kid is struggling in a subject.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.421
You figure out a way
to get 'em up to speed.

00:16:45.421 --> 00:16:46.875
You know, you got a argument
with your girlfriend,

00:16:46.875 --> 00:16:48.394
or your boyfriend,

00:16:48.394 --> 00:16:51.324
you're not going to let this
person walk away, unhappy.

00:16:51.324 --> 00:16:52.755
Like, you all going to figure it out.

00:16:52.755 --> 00:16:53.588
You know what I mean?

00:16:53.588 --> 00:16:54.482
That's winning in life.

00:16:54.482 --> 00:16:55.422
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:16:55.422 --> 00:16:57.570
There's a conflict at work, you handle it.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.879
You step up and handle it.

00:16:58.879 --> 00:17:00.389
You're winning at life,
you know what I mean?

00:17:00.389 --> 00:17:02.269
And that's what it's all
about, bein' a winner,

00:17:02.269 --> 00:17:03.671
at life, at everything.

